Z||000000||raceknb||03-01-99||09:09 PM||||I have an 86.5 Gt and it seems to have a bit of electrical problems.  1st  the temp guage reads between 220 and redline during high speed driving.  The engine bay is not hot, and I have recently done a flush and fill and replace the thermostat according to the chilton guide.  Is this normal.<br>Second  the batt guage is reading 18+volts without the engine running.  and stays there when I start.<br>3rd, the oil pressure guage flutters between 40psi and redline.  Also...mileage is poor.  Only got 110 miles out of the last tank.  Any help would be appreciated.
Z||000001||PaUL||03-09-99||02:14 PM||||About your excessive temp reading, is your radiator fan turning on? I discovered that the stock fan sensor/switch doesnt turn on until the engine is almost boiling over.  
